# What the object-model witness study (study/r2/gap-object-model-witness.md) found. Sources are under 2.20; the 2000 thesis text is 2.3.1. Files of the 2000 archive lie outside every repository and are cited through the report, 2.20.1.

n: 3.12
name: object-model-witness
kind: hub
is: Gap G6, answered by reading alone. 2000: the reference pair (interface id, object id, native flag) is built and six run logs count casts and interface forwards; the delegated calls that let self and the structural base be different objects are compiled (64 stubs) with zero logged runs. 2026: a second class base is flattened into one record; its fixture stood under a pinned Verdict 119 on 2026-09-15 and was cut 2026-09-29; casts are absent. Separate base objects with self kept have no record of running in either era. Templates by substitution ran in both.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-object-model-witness

n: 3.12.1
name: model-2000
kind: hub
is: What the 2000 object model specifies and what its machine and compiler source implement: a reference of two 32-bit table indices with a native flag; a frame carrying a behavioural base (self) and a structural base (this); each additional class parent as a hidden delegated field with forwarding stubs; a cast that rewrites only the interface index. Shared inheritance as an attribute, tagging and detached interfaces are specified and not implemented. Undo rebuilds self instead of saving it.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-object-model-witness

n: 3.12.1.1
name: reference-spec-2000
kind: observation
is: The 2000 object model prescribes one data type, the reference: an object identifier, an interface identifier and a native flag. Both identifiers are 32-bit indices into the object look-up table; the flag is the top bit of the interface identifier; a native reference holds a 32-bit value in place of the object identifier and cannot be aliased.
status: observed
src: 2.20.2#486 2.20.2#490-495 2.20.3#93
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-object-model-witness

n: 3.12.1.2
name: reference-and-cast-built-2000
kind: observation
is: The 2000 machine source makes a reference two unsigned 32-bit indices, interface then object, into one table, native flag 0x80000000 on the interface word; an interface is an object in that table. A cast matches 128-bit GUIDs along the instantiator's interface list and rewrites only the interface index; nothing adds an interface at cast time.
status: observed
src: 2.20.1#93-108 2.20.1#222-226 2.20.2#649-651
limit: The machine source lies in a 2000 archive on local disk outside the repositories. The study read it there and the encoding pass reread the reference struct, the flag and the cast routine. Not run.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-object-model-witness

n: 3.12.1.3
name: two-base-rule-spec
kind: observation
is: The 2000 object model gives every method two base references: the behavioural base (self) always dispatches methods and the structural base (this) always reads fields. A call on an object sets both to it; forwarding to a delegated base sets only the structural base, so a base's method calling through self reaches the derived class's override.
status: observed
src: 2.20.2#642-644 2.20.2#711-713 2.20.2#719-738 2.20.3#103
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-object-model-witness

n: 3.12.1.4
name: frame-forms-2000
kind: observation
is: Every 2000 machine frame holds refSelf, refThis and refMethod, and fields are read through refThis. A send sets both to the target and a self call resets refThis to self; a super call keeps self and changes only the interface half of refThis; only the delegated call CALLD and the forwarding stub FDC move refThis to another object, keeping self.
status: observed
src: 2.20.1#136-160
limit: The machine source lies in a 2000 archive on local disk outside the repositories. The study read it there, the encoding pass reread the frame struct and the CALLD handlers, and the correction pass reread the frame struct and the super, CALLD and FDC handlers (BMCPU/CPU/instructions.hpp:100-162, 1169-1285, 1317-1392). Not run.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-object-model-witness

n: 3.12.1.5
name: undo-rebuilds-self-2000
kind: observation
is: On return the 2000 machine pushes a frame onto the backtrack stack from refThis onward, leaving refSelf out. Re-entry under backtracking pops the frame and sets self to the structural base unless the calling instruction was a delegated call: the flag is false for CALL and true for CALLD. The forwarding instruction FDC refuses both redo and undo.
status: observed
src: 2.20.1#166-173
limit: The machine source lies in a 2000 archive on local disk outside the repositories. The encoding pass reread the push and the restore routine there; the redo flags and the FDC refusal were read by the study only. Not run.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-object-model-witness

n: 3.12.1.6
name: two-base-rule-and-undo-not-jointly-sound
kind: finding
is: In the 2000 machine source the two-base rule and undo do not compose. Re-entering a callee reached through a forwarding stub restores self to the delegate; re-entering a super callee restores self with the base interface's id; re-entering a callee of a delegated call keeps whatever the uninitialised stack slot held.
status: inferred
conf: low
from: 3.12.1.4 3.12.1.5
limit: Inferred from about thirty lines of source. Not run, and no log shows the path taken; the study says it could be wrong about what the stack slot holds.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-object-model-witness

n: 3.12.1.7
name: inheritance-kinds-specified-2000
kind: observation
is: The 2000 texts allow one structural parent; each additional class parent generates a delegated field whose interfaces join the class. The inheritance attributes delegate and shared are marked 'Not supported yet'; shared inheritance 'lacks applications', tagging lacks its normalization mechanism and detached interfaces lack language constructs.
status: observed
src: 2.3.1#234 2.3.1#656-657 2.3.1#722-723 2.20.2#744-749 2.20.2#752-775 2.20.2#787-791
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-object-model-witness

n: 3.12.1.8
name: compiler-2000-delegation-mechanism
kind: observation
is: The 2000 compiler makes each extra class parent a hidden delegate field filled from a constructor parameter, with a stub (fdc field; fcx method) per delegated method not overridden; common objects use the same field. A super-class clause carries a property list, of which the class code reads only class; none spells delegate or shared inheritance.
status: observed
src: 2.20.1#201-218
limit: The report's line 219 says the super-class rule carries no property list; the archive grammar shows one (Java/jbml/JBML.BMF:42, 44, 157). A super class marked class moves to the common object's parents (Components/Class.java:177-184); delegate is a member property and shared an array property (JBML.BMF:149, 137), and no super-class loop of Class.java reads either (177-184, 196-200, 346-356, 495-521, 561-572); other compiler files were not searched for reads of a super class's properties. The compiler source lies in a 2000 archive on local disk outside the repositories; the correction pass reread these lines, the delegated-field maker and the stub maker there. Not run.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-object-model-witness

n: 3.12.2
name: body-2026
kind: hub
is: What the 2026 thesis-lane compiler does with classes: one Form record holds a class id and every field of the whole depth-first base chain; one receiver stands for self, the structural base and super; dispatch reads the class id through an if-chain. A second class base is therefore flattened, with no separate base object. A field marked delegate re-sends the call to the field's value, which makes the delegate the receiver. A cast is parsed and never performed.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-object-model-witness

n: 3.12.2.1
name: one-record-holds-whole-chain
kind: observation
is: In the 2026 thesis compiler the first super is the structural base and later class supers are delegation bases; lookup runs the class, then each super in order, depth first. An instance is one Form record: bmlClass, bmlClassId and every field of that chain, delegation bases included. From outside, a field resolves along the structural chain only.
status: observed
src: 2.20.4#219-220 2.20.4#3339-3371 2.20.4#4254-4257 2.20.5#639-645
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-object-model-witness

n: 3.12.2.2
name: one-receiver-class-id-dispatch
kind: observation
is: A 2026 class member is one function over a packed list whose head is the receiver; self, the structural base and super all lower to that head. A signature that classes answer differently gets a stub that reads bmlClassId from the head and walks an if-chain, one row per class id. A reference carries no interface id.
status: observed
src: 2.20.5#598-610 2.20.5#633 2.20.5#683-685 2.20.4#4279-4291
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-object-model-witness

n: 3.12.2.3
name: delegate-field-resend-and-no-cast
kind: observation
is: For a 2026 field marked delegate, a call its class does not answer is lowered on the field's value. A cast is parsed and never performed: the word stands on 13 lines of the grammar file and none of the lowering file. Three definitions modelling a self class and a structural class stand in the grammar file; no other file of the head tree names them.
status: observed
src: 2.20.4#3634-3647 2.20.4#3679-3683 2.20.5#632 2.20.4#1057 2.20.4#353-356 2.20.4#648-668
