at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-object-model-witness

n: 3.12.4.2
name: logs-2000-no-delegated-call
kind: observation
is: None of the six 2000 instruction-count logs has a row for the delegated call CALLD or the delegated forward FDC, and the logger skips a timer of the requested group only when its count is 0. The two instructions that make self and the structural base name different objects therefore have zero recorded executions.
status: observed
src: 2.20.1#335
limit: The absence of rows and the logger's skip rule are observed; zero executions is inferred from the two, every instruction timer being in group 0. A super call also makes the two references differ, in the interface half only, and has 44 to 281 recorded executions per log. The encoding pass and the correction pass reread the six logs and the skip lines (BMCPU/CPU/performance.cpp:22-23, instruction.hpp:165) in the archive on local disk outside the repositories.
