n: 3.12.5
name: formulation
kind: hub
is: The study's restatement of the object model as cells, offered as a formulation and not a decision: six kinds of node (structure blueprint, interface blueprint, recipe, view, maker, cell); multiple inheritance, sharing, tagging and detached interfaces as uses of delegate slots and a view memo; and one unresolved point, that the cell half of a reference cannot be a content hash of mutable state.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-object-model-witness

n: 3.12.5.1
name: six-node-kinds
kind: finding
is: The 2000 object model restates as six node kinds: structure blueprint (ordered slots, one prefix parent), interface blueprint (ordered recipe signatures, one prefix parent), recipe (method body), view (the recipe-id table of one interface blueprint and maker), maker (the instantiator, which mints cells) and cell (state, one content node per slot).
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.12.1.1 3.12.1.2 1.2 1.4
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-object-model-witness

n: 3.12.5.2
name: features-as-delegate-slots
kind: finding
is: Multiple inheritance is one prefix parent plus delegate slots, with a forwarding recipe per unanswered signature; shared inheritance is two cells whose delegate slots hold one reference; tagging is a new cell delegating to an existing reference; a detached interface is a view computed at cast time and memoised under interface id and maker id.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.12.1.7 3.12.1.8 3.12.1.2 3.12.5.1
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-object-model-witness

n: 3.12.5.3
name: cell-id-cannot-be-content-hash
kind: finding
is: A reference pair needs a cell id that stays while slot contents change, and axiom 3 makes identity the present content. The 2000 answer was an index into a table of mutable descriptors. The cell id cannot be a content hash of the state and has to be a name-like handle; a view, fixed by interface id and maker id, can be content-addressed.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 1.3 3.12.1.1 3.12.1.2
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-object-model-witness

n: 3.12.8
name: keep
kind: hub
is: Seven things to carry forward: the reference as two ids (cell, view) with an immediate mode; an activation carrying self and a structural base under six dispatch rules, with slots reachable only through the structural base; views as memoised facts, with super and casts as operations on the view half; the maker as an ordinary cell; flattening as an optimisation with a stated side condition; templates as recipes from blueprints to blueprints; and the fixture door with the 2000 sources as a conformance corpus.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-object-model-witness

n: 3.12.8.1
name: keep-reference-as-cell-and-view
kind: finding
is: Keep the reference as two ids, cell (whose state) and view (through which interface), or an immediate that carries a value and a view id and names no cell. State holds no table pointer, so a cell's content is the same through every view; identity of the object is equality of the cell id alone.
status: inferred
conf: high
from: 3.12.1.1 3.12.1.2 3.12.4.1
see: 2.20.2#493 2.20.2#701
at: 2026-11-24
