n: 3.12.9
name: drop
kind: hub
is: Four things to let go: the claim that multiple inheritance and the reference pair are proven working; a class id stored inside the record with an if-chain per signature as the dispatch form; a pinned count or a support list as a standing witness; and self reconstructed on undo instead of saved. The study's list also lets go bounds as unchecked syntax, three meanings of class and of template across three readers, and forwarding stubs stored as two-instruction methods per class.
